IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23): the RELATED PROVISIONS (src:3599-4000), the nouns they share.
-- Written by piece ei7 (Sonnet 5.5). Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation
-- current to 2026-09-30; nothing here claims to be verified against the official text.
-- Nouns only (skill step 4): no rule is defined here. Every other ei7 module imports this one.
-- Rule names in ei7 modules begin "Act RP", for "related provision of the Act", so that they cannot clash with
-- piece er6, which meets two of the same amending provisions (2009, c. 2, s. 226 and 2009, c. 30, s. 7) in the
-- Regulations' file. Types and constructors begin "ei7".

§ `Provisions that a transitional section lists`

-- Five transitional sections (2016, c. 7, ss. 225 to 227; 2021, c. 23, ss. 332 and 335; 2022, c. 10, s. 411) list
-- provisions of the Employment Insurance Act whose earlier text keeps applying, or whose new text applies only
-- from a day. The constructors are the Act's own units of citation, one per distinct unit the lists use: where
-- two lists cut a provision differently ("subsection 21(1)" in 332(e), "section 21" in 335(e)) there are two
-- constructors, because the texts do not say that one contains the other as the lists name them (fork F12).
-- src:3795 | — 2016, c. 7, s. 225
-- src:3796 | Provisions continue to apply
-- src:3797 | 225 The following provisions of the Employment Insurance Act, as those provisions read immediately before July 9, 2017, continue to apply in respect of a claimant, as defined in subsection 2(1) of that Act, whose benefit period, as defined in that subsection 2(1), began before that day and has not ended before that day:
-- src:3798 | (a) the definition long-tenured worker in subsection 2(1);
-- src:3799 | (b) subsections 10(13.1) to (14.1); and
-- src:3800 | (c) subsections 12(2) to (2.8) and (6).
-- src:3802 | — 2016, c. 7, s. 226
-- src:3803 | Application of provisions
-- src:3804 | 226 The following provisions of the Employment Insurance Act, as enacted by subsections 207(3), 209(1) and 210(1) and (3) and section 220, apply only in respect of a claimant, as defined in subsection 2(1) of that Act, whose benefit period, as defined in that subsection 2(1), begins on or after the day fixed by order of the Governor in Council made under subsection 231(3):
-- src:3805 | (a) subsection 2(5);
-- src:3806 | (b) the portion of subsection 7(2) before paragraph (a);
