§ `Bands of the day a benefit period begins`

-- 2021, c. 23, ss. 332 to 335 and 2022, c. 10, s. 411 all test the day a benefit period begins against the same
-- three days: September 27, 2020, September 26, 2021 and September 25, 2022. Four bands result. The band is a
-- noun of this range; the rule that places a day in its band is in ei7-related-2020-2023.
-- src:3928 | 332 The following provisions of the Employment Insurance Act, as they read immediately before September 26, 2021, continue to apply in respect of an insured person or a claimant, as the case may be, whose benefit period begins before that day:
-- src:3947 | 333 Part VIII.5 of the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before September 26, 2021, continues to apply in respect of an insured person or claimant, as the case may be, whose benefit period begins during the period beginning on September 27, 2020 and ending on September 25, 2021.
-- src:3951 | 334 (1) The operation of Part VIII.1 of the Employment Insurance Act and any regulations made under that Part is suspended during the period beginning on September 26, 2021 and ending on September 24, 2022.
-- src:3957 | 335 The following provisions of the Employment Insurance Act, as they read immediately before September 25, 2022, continue to apply in respect of an insured person or a claimant, as the case may be, whose benefit period begins during the period beginning on September 26, 2021 and ending on September 24, 2022:
-- src:3984 | 411 Schedule V to the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before September 25, 2022, continues to apply in respect of a claimant whose benefit period, as those terms are defined in subsection 2(1) of that Act, begins before September 25, 2022.
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provisions of 2021, c. 23, ss. 332 to 335 and 2022, c. 10, s. 411 (src:3928) (src:3947) (src:3951) (src:3957) (src:3984)
DECLARE `ei7 Band of the day a benefit period begins` IS ONE OF
    `ei7 begins before September 27, 2020`
    `ei7 begins from September 27, 2020 to September 25, 2021`
    `ei7 begins from September 26, 2021 to September 24, 2022`
    `ei7 begins on or after September 25, 2022`

§ `Bodies named in the transitional provisions about appeals`

-- 2012, c. 19, s. 251 defines five bodies and 2023, c. 26, s. 664 defines five more; they overlap in the
-- Social Security Tribunal, which s. 664 calls "the Tribunal", and in the General Division and the Appeal Division
-- of the Tribunal, which the 2012 sections name without defining. One constructor for each distinct body.
-- src:3694 | — 2012, c. 19, s. 251
-- src:3695 | Definitions
-- src:3696 | 251 The following definitions apply in sections 252 to 270.
-- src:3697 | board of referees means a board of referees established under Part VI of the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 247. (conseil arbitral)
-- src:3698 | Pension Appeals Board means the Pension Appeals Board established under section 83 of the Canada Pension Plan, as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 229. (Commission d’appel des pensions)
-- src:3699 | Review Tribunal means a Review Tribunal established under section 82 of the Canada Pension Plan, as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 229. (tribunal de révision)
-- src:3700 | Social Security Tribunal means the Social Security Tribunal established under section 44 of the Department of Human Resources and Skills Development Act. (Tribunal de la sécurité sociale)
-- src:3701 | umpire means an umpire appointed under Part VI of the Employment Insurance Act, as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 247. (juge-arbitre)
-- src:3986 | — 2023, c. 26, s. 664
-- src:3987 | Definitions
-- src:3988 | 664 The following definitions apply in this section and sections 665 to 678.
-- src:3989 | Appeal Division means the Appeal Division of the Tribunal. (division d’appel)
-- src:3990 | Board of Appeal means the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal established under section 43.01 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act. (Conseil d’appel)
-- src:3991 | Employment Insurance Section means the Employment Insurance Section of the General Division. (section de l’assurance-emploi)
-- src:3992 | General Division means, except for the purposes of subsections 665(2) and 667(2), the General Division referred to in section 44 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act, as it reads on the day on which this section comes into force. (division générale)
-- src:3993 | Tribunal means the Social Security Tribunal established under section 44 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act. (Tribunal)
@ref Employment Insurance Act, related provisions of 2012, c. 19, s. 251 and 2023, c. 26, s. 664 (src:3694-3701) (src:3986-3993)
DECLARE `ei7 Body named in a transitional provision about appeals` IS ONE OF
    `ei7 the board of referees`
    `ei7 the Pension Appeals Board`
    `ei7 a Review Tribunal`
    `ei7 an umpire`
    `ei7 the Social Security Tribunal`
    `ei7 the General Division of the Social Security Tribunal`
    `ei7 the Appeal Division of the Social Security Tribunal`
    `ei7 the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal`
    `ei7 the Employment Insurance Section of the General Division`
